

/// Reverse a String

const reverseString = str => [...str].reverse().join('');

console.log(reverseString('hello')); // OUTPUT : olleh
console.log(reverseString('Java script')); // OUTPUT : tpircs avaJ


const reverseString creates a function named reverseString.
[...'hello'] --> This is called the spread syntax (or) Spread Operator.It takes the characters of a string and spreads them into an array.Think of it like taking a word apart and putting each character into its own box.

The .join('') method joins all array elements into a single string.
.join('') — joins characters without anything between them.
.join('-') — joins characters with a hyphen between them.

['o', 'l', 'l', 'e', 'h'].join('')
// "olleh"
// ['o', 'l', 'l', 'e', 'h'].join('-')
// "o-l-l-e-h"
